    "id": "/lh/en/mobile-app/non-destination/what-the-hack--flying-with-kids-–-tips-for-relaxed-family-flights",
    "items": [
     {
      "type": "mainHeadline",
      "text": "What the Hack: Flying With Kids – Tips for Relaxed Family Flights",
      "variant": "HEADING_XL",
      "id": "/lh/en/mobile-app/non-destination/what-the-hack--flying-with-kids-–-tips-for-relaxed-family-flights_title",
      "isBold": true
     },
     {
      "type": "copyText",
      "text": "<b>9. October 2025 | 5 min read | Stefanie Pröstler-Meckl</b>",
      "size": "SMALL",
      "variant": "BODY",
      "id": "/lh/en/mobile-app/non-destination/what-the-hack--flying-with-kids-–-tips-for-relaxed-family-flights_info"
     },
     {
      "type": "copyText",
      "text": "<b>Flying with kids can be exciting – and sometimes a bit challenging. Stefanie Pröstler-Meckl knows this all too well. On Instagram, the world traveler shares what she and her husband experience while flying with their two children.</b>",
      "size": "MEDIUM",
      "variant": "BODY",
      "id": "/lh/en/mobile-app/non-destination/what-the-hack--flying-with-kids-–-tips-for-relaxed-family-flights_description_0"
     },
     {
      "type": "spacer",
      "size": "MEDIUM",
      "id": "/lh/en/mobile-app/non-destination/what-the-hack--flying-with-kids-–-tips-for-relaxed-family-flights_separator"
     },
     {
      "type": "copyText",
      "text": "<b>Joy Over Stress: Get Excited Before You Board</b>",
      "size": "MEDIUM",
      "variant": "BODY",
      "id": "/lh/en/mobile-app/non-destination/what-the-hack--flying-with-kids-–-tips-for-relaxed-family-flights_paragraph_0"
     },
     {
      "type": "copyText",
      "text": "Travel starts in the mind – with excitement! Kids should know beforehand how fun and adventurous flying can be. Even if you're feeling a bit nervous, it's better to show curiosity and confidence than to pass on your own worries. One great trick is to read a picture book about flying. Many children's books explain things like security checks, boarding, and the aircraft interior in a fun and playful way.",
      "size": "MEDIUM",
      "variant": "BODY",
      "id": "/lh/en/mobile-app/non-destination/what-the-hack--flying-with-kids-–-tips-for-relaxed-family-flights_paragraph_1"
     },
     {
      "type": "image",
      "id": "/content/mobile/lh/en/articles/what-the-hack-travel-with-kids/jcr:content/articlecontentfragment/par1/image",
      "url": "https://www.lufthansa.com/content/dam/lufthansa-group/poi/de/images/local_images/blog_article_img/what-the-hack-travel-with-kids/lh_blog_eva_explora_1920x823.jpg.transform/lh-dcep-transform-width-1440/img.jpg",
      "contentDescription": "Mom with two kids at the sea and at the airport with suitcases"
     },
     {
      "type": "spacer",
      "size": "MEDIUM",
      "id": "/content/mobile/lh/en/articles/what-the-hack-travel-with-kids/jcr:content/articlecontentfragment/par1/separator_copy_copy"
     },
     {
      "type": "copyText",
      "text": "<b>Play Before Takeoff</b>",
      "size": "MEDIUM",
      "variant": "BODY",
      "id": "/lh/en/mobile-app/non-destination/what-the-hack--flying-with-kids-–-tips-for-relaxed-family-flights_paragraph_2"
     },
     {
      "type": "copyText",
      "text": "Before expecting your kids to sit still on the plane, let them run wild at the airport. Most big airports – and many smaller ones – have designated kids' zones. If you arrive early and don't mind a bit of walking, you can seek out the best ones, such as those in Munich, Zurich, or Copenhagen, where some even have views of the runway. Pro tip: bring spare socks because many play areas require them.",
      "size": "MEDIUM",
      "variant": "BODY",
      "id": "/lh/en/mobile-app/non-destination/what-the-hack--flying-with-kids-–-tips-for-relaxed-family-flights_paragraph_3"
     },
     {
      "type": "image",
      "id": "/content/mobile/lh/en/articles/what-the-hack-travel-with-kids/jcr:content/articlecontentfragment/par3/image",
      "url": "https://www.lufthansa.com/content/dam/lufthansa-group/poi/de/images/local_images/blog_article_img/what-the-hack-travel-with-kids/lh_blog_father_and_son_airport_gettyimages_1150687457.jpg.transform/lh-dcep-transform-width-1440/img.jpg",
      "contentDescription": "Father and child playing with toy plane at airport gate"
     },
     {
      "type": "spacer",
      "size": "MEDIUM",
      "id": "/content/mobile/lh/en/articles/what-the-hack-travel-with-kids/jcr:content/articlecontentfragment/par3/separator_copy_copy"
     },
     {
      "type": "copyText",
      "text": "<b>\"Kids should know beforehand how fun and adventurous flying can be.\"<br> </b>Stefanie Pröstler-Meckl",
      "size": "MEDIUM",
      "variant": "BODY",
      "id": "/lh/en/mobile-app/non-destination/what-the-hack--flying-with-kids-–-tips-for-relaxed-family-flights_paragraph_4"
     },
     {
      "type": "copyText",
      "text": "<b>Smart Packing Makes for Smooth Flying</b>",
      "size": "MEDIUM",
      "variant": "BODY",
      "id": "/lh/en/mobile-app/non-destination/what-the-hack--flying-with-kids-–-tips-for-relaxed-family-flights_paragraph_5"
     },
     {
      "type": "copyText",
      "text": "More is more: bring plenty of (minimally sweetened) snacks to keep little ones happy and wel-fed in the air. If you're short on prep time, you can preorder the Onboard Delights Kids Box with child-friendly snacks on the Lufthansa website up to 24 hours before your flight.",
      "size": "MEDIUM",
      "variant": "BODY",
      "id": "/lh/en/mobile-app/non-destination/what-the-hack--flying-with-kids-–-tips-for-relaxed-family-flights_paragraph_6"
     },
     {
      "type": "image",
      "id": "/content/mobile/lh/en/articles/what-the-hack-travel-with-kids/jcr:content/articlecontentfragment/par6/image",
      "url": "https://www.lufthansa.com/content/dam/lufthansa-group/poi/de/images/local_images/blog_article_img/what-the-hack-travel-with-kids/lh_blog_family_packing_gettyimages_1587648424_1920x823.jpg.transform/lh-dcep-transform-width-1440/img.jpg",
      "contentDescription": "Open suitcase being packed with kids' clothes and a stuffed toy"
     },
     {
      "type": "spacer",
      "size": "MEDIUM",
      "id": "/content/mobile/lh/en/articles/what-the-hack-travel-with-kids/jcr:content/articlecontentfragment/par6/separator_copy_copy"
     },
     {
      "type": "copyText",
      "text": "<b>Pressure? No Problem!</b>",
      "size": "MEDIUM",
      "variant": "BODY",
      "id": "/lh/en/mobile-app/non-destination/what-the-hack--flying-with-kids-–-tips-for-relaxed-family-flights_paragraph_7"
     },
     {
      "type": "copyText",
      "text": "Changes in cabin pressure during takeoff and landing can be unpleasant – especially for kids. To avoid sore ears, encourage chewing, drinking, or sucking. For babies, that means breastfeeding, a bottle, or a pacifier. For older kids, try straw cups or chewing gum.",
      "size": "MEDIUM",
      "variant": "BODY",
      "id": "/lh/en/mobile-app/non-destination/what-the-hack--flying-with-kids-–-tips-for-relaxed-family-flights_paragraph_8"
     },
     {
      "type": "image",
      "id": "/content/mobile/lh/en/articles/what-the-hack-travel-with-kids/jcr:content/articlecontentfragment/par8/image",
      "url": "https://www.lufthansa.com/content/dam/lufthansa-group/poi/de/images/local_images/blog_article_img/what-the-hack-travel-with-kids/lh_blog_girl_drinking_water_gettyimages_1465217065_1920x823.jpg.transform/lh-dcep-transform-width-1440/img.jpg",
      "contentDescription": "Girl with headphones drinking water on an airplane seat"
     },
     {
      "type": "spacer",
      "size": "MEDIUM",
      "id": "/content/mobile/lh/en/articles/what-the-hack-travel-with-kids/jcr:content/articlecontentfragment/par8/separator_copy_copy"
     },
     {
      "type": "copyText",
      "text": "<b>Never Without a Spare Shirt</b>",
      "size": "MEDIUM",
      "variant": "BODY",
      "id": "/lh/en/mobile-app/non-destination/what-the-hack--flying-with-kids-–-tips-for-relaxed-family-flights_paragraph_9"
     },
     {
      "type": "copyText",
      "text": "On long-haul flights, I always pack a change of clothes – and not just for the kids. I toss in a fresh T-shirt and comfy leggings for myself too. When you're flying with kids, something is bound to go wrong. There might be a spilled juice, a diaper disaster, or an unexpected cuddle-slobber attack. Bonus tip: pack spare clothes in a separate pouch so you can grab them quickly without digging through everything.",
      "size": "MEDIUM",
      "variant": "BODY",
      "id": "/lh/en/mobile-app/non-destination/what-the-hack--flying-with-kids-–-tips-for-relaxed-family-flights_paragraph_10"
     },
     {
      "type": "spacer",
      "size": "MEDIUM",
      "id": "/content/mobile/lh/en/articles/what-the-hack-travel-with-kids/jcr:content/articlecontentfragment/par10/separator_copy_copy_"
     },
